TEXT:
CSRU Admit note
Pt admitted to CSRU after asystolic event on [**Hospital Ward Name **] 2; Pt was nauseous and slightly hypotensive on floor, placed in bed, brady down and 10 second asystolic period, agonal resps, bagged and self converted to NSR w/ectopy; Transferred to CSRU on CCU service for observation; Scheduled for CABG x3 on Monday;
Neuro: Alert and oriented x3; MAE w/normal strength; PERL-no neuro deficits;
CV: NSR w/frequent multifocal PVC's-electrolytes repleted, CCU team aware; Skin warm and dry, pulses palpable; BP stable;
Resp: 2 L NC; Lungs cl w/crackles @ R base; Resps unlabored; Sats 98 or better;
GI: Active BS; Denies nausea; ABD soft; Fair appetite; BM this evening;
GU: Foley in place, urine output adequate;
Pain: Denies pain;
Activity: Bedrest, OOB w/assist;
Plan: Cont to monitor EKG/hemodynamics; Activity as tol; Pre-op procedures tomorrow;
